2.Custom Exceptions

Define domain-specific exceptions:

public class ResourceNotFoundException extends RuntimeException {
    public ResourceNotFoundException(String message) {
        super(message);
    }
}

public class FileStorageException extends RuntimeException {
    public FileStorageException(String message) {
        super(message);
    }
}

Makes it easy to map specific errors to proper HTTP status codes.

3.Handle Validation Errors

Use @Valid in controllers with DTOs:

@PostMapping("/users")
public ResponseEntity<UserDto> createUser(@Valid @RequestBody UserDto user) {
    UserDto saved = service.save(user);
    return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CREATED).body(saved);
}

Invalid fields trigger MethodArgumentNotValidException, which is caught in GlobalExceptionHandler.


