how can enable specific environment without using profile or what is the alternative to profile to achieve same use case

-->
Property-Based Conditional Configuration (Most Common Alternative)

Instead of profiles, use properties as feature/environment switches.

Example: application.yml
app.env: prod
feature.newFlow.enabled: true

Example: application.properties
app.active.env =  prod


Conditional Bean Using @ConditionalOnProperty
@Configuration
public class FeatureConfig {

    @Bean
   @ConditionalOnProperty(     //using this type of annotation
    prefix = "app.active"
    name = "env",
    havingValue = "prod"
)
    public PaymentService newPaymentService() {
        return new NewPaymentService();
    }

    @Bean
    @ConditionalOnProperty(
        name = "feature.newFlow.enabled",
        havingValue = "false",
        matchIfMissing = true
    )
    public PaymentService oldPaymentService() {
        return new OldPaymentService();
    }
}
✔ No profiles
✔ Environment controlled via config
✔ Used heavily in production systems


